## 6. Worked Example: Catching a Real Correlated Hallucination

**Scenario**: Invariant `I = ∀addr: balance[addr] ≥ 0` for a token contract. Ten LLM-based verifiers all say "holds." But the contract has an integer-underflow bug that makes balance negative in edge case `transfer_to_self_with_zero_balance`.

**What happens without our gates:**
- All 10 say "holds" → naive majority = confirmed → bug ships.

**What happens with our gates:**

| Gate | Result | Why |
|------|--------|-----|
| 1: Unanimity | ✅ Pass | All say "true" |
| 2: Decoy rejection | ❌ **FAIL** | We planted 3 known-false invariants. All 10 verifiers "confirmed" 2 of 3 decoys because they pattern-match "balance-related → probably fine." Decoy rejection rate = 33% < 90% |
| 3: Path diversity | ⚠️ Would pass | Traces happen to differ slightly |
| 4: Perturbation entropy | ✅ Pass | Different seeds assigned |

**Verdict: `CorrelatedHallucination`** — caught at Gate 2 before any damage.

---

## 7. Why This Is Sound

**Completeness argument**: If verifiers are truly independent with per-verifier error rate ε ≤ 0.1, then:
- P(all N wrong on primary) ≤ εᴺ ≤ 10⁻¹⁰ for N=10
- P(fail decoy gate) = P(any verifier accepts a known-false invariant) — independent verifiers with ε≤0.1 will reject decoys with prob ≥0.9 each, so collective rejection rate ≥0.9 w.h.p.
- P(path traces identical) ≈ 0 for independent reasoners (astronomically unlikely to derive same sequence)

**Soundness argument**: If verifiers ARE correlated (ρ→1), then:
- They share the same blind spots → fail same decoys → Gate 2 fires
- They follow same reasoning template → Gate 3 fires
- They anchor to same surface features → perturbation reveals this at Gate 4/5

At least one gate fires for any realistic correlation mode. The system never confirms a hallucinated consensus.

---

## 8. Summary Table

| Component | Specification |
|-----------|--------------|
| Input type | `ConsensusRound` (deterministically serializable) |
| Output type | `ConsensusVerdict` (3-valued enum) |
| State delta | Exactly one `(canonical_hash, old_status, new_status)` |
| Gates | 5 sequential, short-circuit on first failure |
| Determinism | Pure function, no RNG, no wall-clock, no network |
| Byte-identity proof | 100-run hash-collision test + canonical serialization test |
| False-positive rate | ≤ εᴺ for independent verifiers |
| Detection power | Catches correlated hallucination whenever decoys or path-homogeneity expose it |
